acker to \nforge requests by compromising logback configuration files in XML.\n\n\n\nThe attacks involves the modification of DOCTYPE declaration in  XML configuration files.","Severity":"LOW","CweIDs":["CWE-918"],"VendorSeverity":{"ghsa":1,"redhat":1},"CVSS":{"ghsa":{"V40Vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H/V:D/U:Clear","V40Score":2.4},"redhat":{"V3Vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","V3Score":3.3}},"References":["https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2024-12801","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/5f05041cba4c4ac0a62748c5c527a2da48999f2d","https://logback.qos.ch/news.html#1.3.15","https://logback.qos.ch/news.html#1.5.13","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2024-12801","https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-12801"],"PublishedDate":"2024-12-19T17:15:08.93Z","LastModifiedDate":"2026-06-17T07:00:31.467Z"},{"VulnerabilityID":"CVE-2026-10532","VendorIDs":["GHSA-jhq6-gfmj-v8fx"],"PkgID":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core:1.5.12","PkgName":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core","PkgIdentifier":{"PURL":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar","UID":"7ee2b4efef1a78ed","BOMRef":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar"},"InstalledVersion":"1.5.12","FixedVersion":"1.5.34","Status":"fixed","SeveritySource":"ghsa","PrimaryURL":"https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-10532","DataSource":{"ID":"ghsa","Name":"GitHub Security Advisory Maven","URL":"https://github.com/advisories?query=type%3Areviewed+ecosystem%3Amaven"},"Fingerprint":"sha256:0d50c860c312fe31e58d7650e7eac78c9381f002744d952e2398440efb92ab42","Title":"Deserialization of untrusted data vulnerability in QOS.CH Sarl logback ...","Description":"Deserialization of untrusted data vulnerability in QOS.CH Sarl logback logback-core (HardenedObjectInputStream (logback-core) modules) allows Object Injection, albeit heavily restricted.\n\nMore precisely, an attacker able to influence serialized data sent to \nSimpleSocketServer or SimpleSSLSocketServer can instantiate Proxy objects.\n\n\nAlthough deserialization is heavily restricted by HardenedObjectInputStream and no \npractical way to achieve remote code execution or significant privilege \nescalation has been identified, this issue constitutes a bypass of the \nintended security restrictions.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects logback: through 1.5.33 inclusive.","Severity":"LOW","CweIDs":["CWE-502"],"VendorSeverity":{"ghsa":1},"CVSS":{"ghsa":{"V40Vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N/E:P/RE:M/U:Green","V40Score":2.9}},"References":["https://advisory.echohq.com/cve/CVE-2026-10532","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/releases/tag/v_1.5.34","https://logback.qos.ch/news.html#1.5.34","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-10532"],"PublishedDate":"2026-06-01T13:16:30.34Z","LastModifiedDate":"2026-07-22T07:10:00.107Z"},{"VulnerabilityID":"CVE-2026-1225","VendorIDs":["GHSA-qqpg-mvqg-649v"],"PkgID":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core:1.5.12","PkgName":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core","PkgIdentifier":{"PURL":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar","UID":"7ee2b4efef1a78ed","BOMRef":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar"},"InstalledVersion":"1.5.12","FixedVersion":"1.5.25","Status":"fixed","SeveritySource":"ghsa","PrimaryURL":"https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-1225","DataSource":{"ID":"ghsa","Name":"GitHub Security Advisory Maven","URL":"https://github.com/advisories?query=type%3Areviewed+ecosystem%3Amaven"},"Fingerprint":"sha256:2eb2af899140828631ff6a927bdf88f3885f4bb93f9c584ffc499f964193c008","Title":"ch.qos.logback/logback-core: Malicious logback.xml configuration file allows instantiation of arbitrary classes","Description":"ACE vulnerability in configuration file processing  by QOS.CH logback-core up to and including version 1.5.24 in Java applications, allows an attacker to instantiate classes already present on the class path by compromising an existing logback configuration file.\n\n\n\n\nThe instantiation of a potentially malicious Java class requires that said class is present on the user's class-path. In addition, the attacker must  have write access to a \nconfiguration file. However, after successful instantiation, the instance is very likely to be discarded with no further ado.","Severity":"LOW","CweIDs":["CWE-20"],"VendorSeverity":{"ghsa":1,"redhat":2},"CVSS":{"ghsa":{"V40Vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:L/SI:L/SA:L","V40Score":1.8},"redhat":{"V3Vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:L","V3Score":5}},"References":["https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-1225","https://advisory.echohq.com/cve/CVE-2026-1225","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qqpg-mvqg-649v","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/1f97ae1844b1be8486e4e9cade98d7123d3eded5","https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/issues/997","https://logback.qos.ch/news.html#1.5.25","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-1225","https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-1225"],"PublishedDate":"2026-01-22T10:16:07.693Z","LastModifiedDate":"2026-06-17T10:15:21.373Z"},{"VulnerabilityID":"CVE-2026-9828","VendorIDs":["GHSA-p47f-322f-whfh"],"PkgID":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core:1.5.12","PkgName":"ch.qos.logback:logback-core","PkgIdentifier":{"PURL":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar","UID":"7ee2b4efef1a78ed","BOMRef":"pkg:maven/ch.qos.logback/logback-core@1.5.12?type=jar"},"InstalledVersion":"1.5.12","FixedVersion":"1.5.33","Status":"fixed","SeveritySource":"ghsa","PrimaryURL":"https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9828","DataSource":{"ID":"ghsa","Name":"GitHub Security Advisory Maven","URL":"https://github.com/advisories?query=type%3Areviewed+ecosystem%3Amaven"},"Fingerprint":"sha256:95aa6f812599b2fec57dc43a80b9bb1008a5861e7c376b5dab7b5034cf579aeb","Title":"Deserialization of untrusted data vulnerability in QOS.CH Sarl logback ...","Description